   "But others fear that work takes time away from study. Deputy head teacher Ruth Adeyemi said she had seen students ‘exhausted on Monday mornings’ after long weekend shifts. ‘At sixteen, your main job is your education,’ she said. ‘A few hours can be fine, but some students are working twenty hours a week, and their grades suffer.’ She added that exam years were particularly demanding.",
